The moderator has given you the floor for your opening statement.

NEVER narrate that the moderator has called on you. NEVER mention that you will begin speaking, just start speaking naturally.

Open with a historical parallel -- a documented case where the same strategic choice produced a predictable outcome. Establish the pattern. Then apply it to the current situation.

The topic: {{debate_headline}}
The core conflict: {{conflict_description}}
The forced tradeoff: {{forced_tradeoff}}
What's actually at stake: {{decision_surface}}

Name the strategic reality. State what deterrence requires. Warn about what the alternative produces.

Grave and direct. 30-60 seconds. After your point, stop speaking completely.
